Description: VA-API video decode driver for Rockchip RK3588 (MPP)
 Hardware video decode on the RK3588/RK3588S video decoders through
 Rockchip MPP, offered to applications through VA-API (libva): H.264,
 HEVC, VP8 and VP9, 8- and 10-bit, with zero-copy DRM PRIME surface
 export (NV12 and P010). The 10-bit conversion runs on the RGA 2D engine.
 Needs a Rockchip BSP kernel that provides /dev/mpp_service.
 .
 Also installs panthor_drv_video.so and panfrost_drv_video.so links so
 libva finds the driver on Panthor/Panfrost GPU stacks. Replaces the
 earlier rockchip-vaapi-driver package.
